error[Z0101]: no variable `fitted` in `top`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:47
  |
4 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(data: top, y: fitted)
  |                                               ^^^^^^ not a variable of top
  |
  = help: the variables of `top` are: worker, year, wage, educ, exper, age, hours, union and 3 more

== neither_maps_y
error[Z0401]: `points` places each mark by its `x` and its `y`, but neither the plot nor this layer maps a variable to `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:17
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ).points(x: exper)
  |                 ^^^^^^ needs both `x` and `y`
  |
  = help: name it in the layer, as in `points(x: educ, y: wage)`, or where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ, y: wage)`

== neither_maps_either
error[Z0401]: `points` places each mark by its `x` and its `y`, but the plot maps no variable to `x` or `y`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:10
  |
3 | d.plot().points(color: union)
  |          ^^^^^^ needs both `x` and `y`
  |
  = help: map both where the plot starts, as in `plot(x: educ, y: wage)`

