== a_variable_in_quotes
error[Z0401]: `color:` of `points` is "union", which is not the name of a colour
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:40
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(color: "union")
  |                                        ^^^^^^^ not a colour
  |
  = help: a string sets one colour for every mark; to colour by the variable `union`, write it without quotation marks, `color: union`

== a_date_for_a_colour
error[Z0401]: `points` shows `color` as categories or on a continuous scale, so `day` must be a Bool, Int, Float, Str or Category variable, but it is a Date
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:110
  |
3 | frame(a = [1, 2], b = [3, 4], day = [date("2026-01-01"), date("2026-01-02")]).plot(x: a, y: b).points(color: day)
  |                                                                                                              ^^^ no colour scale for this type
  |
  = help: a colour scale of dates is not in this release yet; `the frame.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== a_number_where_categories_are
error[Z0401]: the plot shows `union` as categories for `color`, but `hours`, which `points` maps to `color`, is a Float without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:54
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage, color: union).points(color: hours)
  |                                                      ^^^^^ `hours` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one scale of colour, so the variables mapped to `color` must all be categories (a Category, a Str, a Bool or a variable with value labels) or all be numbers without value labels

== categories_where_a_number_is
error[Z0401]: the plot shows `hours` on a continuous scale for `color`, but `union`, which `points` maps to `color`, is an Int with value labels, which is shown as categories
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:54
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage, color: hours).points(color: union)
  |                                                      ^^^^^ `union` is of another kind
  |
  = help: the layers of a plot share one scale of colour, so the variables mapped to `color` must all be categories (a Category, a Str, a Bool or a variable with value labels) or all be numbers without value labels

== another_kind_than_the_first_layer
note: 6 rows with NA in educ or wage dropped (line 3)
error[Z0401]: the plot shows `union` as categories for `color`, but `hours`, which `points` maps to `color`, is a Float without value labels, which is shown on a continuous scale
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:61
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(color: union).points(color: hours)
  |                                                             ^^^^^ `hours` is of another kind
