== categories_for_a_size
error[Z0401]: `points` shows `size` by area, so `union` must be an Int or Float variable without value labels, but it is an Int with value labels
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:39
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(size: union)
  |                                       ^^^^^ not an amount
  |
  = help: a size shows how much: the area of a mark is in proportion to the value; categories are shown by `color:` or `shape:`

== no_size
error[Z0401]: `size:` of `points` is the diameter of every mark in points of 1/72 inch, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:39
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(size: 0)
  |                                       ^ not a size
  |
  = help: write a size such as 3 or 6, or the name of a variable to size the marks by; without `size:` a point takes the size the plot gives, or is 4.5 across

== a_number_for_a_shape
error[Z0401]: `points` gives each category a shape, so `hours` must be a Bool, Str or Category variable, or a number with value labels, but it is a Float without value labels
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:40
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(shape: hours)
  |                                        ^^^^^ not categories
  |
  = help: a shape shows a category; a number is shown by `color:` or `size:`, or made categories first, as in `d.add(hours = category(hours))`

== not_a_shape
error[Z0401]: `shape:` of `points` is "blob", which is not the name of a shape
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:40
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(shape: "blob")
  |                                        ^^^^^^ not a shape
  |
  = help: a shape is one of asterisk, circle, circle_open, cross, diamond, diamond_open, plus, square, square_open, star, star_open, triangle, triangle_down, triangle_down_open and triangle_open

== an_expression_for_a_colour
error[Z0401]: `color:` of `points` takes a variable of the frame or a string, not an expression
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:40
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(color: wage > 20)
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^ an expression
  |
  = help: compute it first on the frame, with `add(v = wage > 20)`, and name the new variable: `.points(color: v)`

== an_expression_for_a_size
error[Z0401]: `size:` of `points` takes a variable of the frame or a number, not an expression
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:39
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(size: hours / 2)
  |                                       ^^^^^^^^^ an expression
  |
  = help: compute it first on the frame, with `add(v = hours / 2)`, and name the new variable: `.points(size: v)`

== an_expression_for_a_shape
error[Z0401]: `shape:` of `points` takes a variable of the frame or a string, not an expression
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:40
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(shape: union == 1)
  |                                        ^^^^^^^^^^ an expression
  |
  = help: compute it first on the frame, with `add(v = union == 1)`, and name the new variable: `.points(shape: v)`

== text_for_a_position
error[Z0401]: `points` draws `y` on a linear scale, so `"fitted"` must give a Bool, Int or Float for each row, but it gives a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:36
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(y: "fitted")
  |                                    ^^^^^^^^ not a number for each row
  |
  = help: the scales of categories, text and dates are not in this release yet; `d.describe()` lists the types of the variables

== no_group_on_a_mark_of_points
error[Z0404]: `points` has no argument called `group`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:33
  |
3 | d.plot(x: educ, y: wage).points(group: union)
  |                                 ^^^^^ unknown argument
  |
  = help: usage: `p.points(data: Frame, x: Var | Expr, y: Var | Expr, color: Var | Str, size: Var | Float, shape: Var | Str, alpha: Float = 1, jitter: Float = 0)`
